1
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:14,431
FROM ME TO YOU 2ND SEASON

2
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:03,063
IMPORTANT PERSON

3
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:12,530
Were you okay?

4
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,244
Huh?

5
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:21,081
With what I said, I mean.

6
00:01:22,832 --> 00:01:23,750
- Oh, uh...
- Oh, uh...

7
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:29,255
Let me hold it. It's a
boyfriend privilege.

8
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,381
Boyfriend?

9
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:32,675
All right, got it!

10
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:36,096
Ahh, no! It should really be my
privilege, since... I'm the one receiving

11
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:39,015
- help.
- Don't be silly.

12
00:01:40,517 --> 00:01:43,228
The privilege is all mine... ...Kuronuma.

13
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:47,816
Because of that...

14
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:48,733
... here...

15
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:52,654
Actually... I-If you don't mind...

16
00:01:53,404 --> 00:01:55,406
...I'll keep this one.

17
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:57,367
So, that way...

18
00:01:58,076 --> 00:02:00,662
...we can go throw them away together.

19
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:13,508
I'm sorry I said that
in front of everyone.

20
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:19,389
I was done hiding it... ...so
before it become a rumor...

21
00:02:19,472 --> 00:02:23,101
...I thought I should
make it perfectly clear...

22
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:26,855
I wanted people to know I really like you.

23
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:29,065
And that we're dating.

24
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:33,027
I... didn't want this to
get more complicated.

25
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:34,988
That's why...

26
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:41,744
Wait! Actually... I already told you my
feelings in front of everyone. But it's

27
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:45,165
not like that was how
I planned on doing it.

28
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:48,626
I'm sorry if I embarrassed you...

29
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:52,255
It made me...

30
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,674
...so happy.

31
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:58,970
He's trying to express his feelings...

32
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:02,724
...so that they're clear
to me and everyone else.

33
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:04,684
Well, I'm glad.

34
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:10,481
Are you two acting out a dating sim
while taking out the trash?! And what's

35
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:13,109
with this sparkly background?!

36
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:15,153
Shoo! Shoo! Get outta here!

37
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:17,488
Come with me, Shota!

38
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:21,034
You're taking Miura's
place! Time to clean!

39
00:03:21,117 --> 00:03:24,287
Kazehaya! You can't tag
along, it defeats the whole point!

40
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:29,918
Listen up... -It's time for you to learn
that however many ups there are in life,

41
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:35,590
there are just as many
downs. -Sorry, Kuronuma!

42
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:38,468
So what people were
saying was really true.

43
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:41,179
- Wait... what?
- I'm shocked.

44
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:44,474
- I refuse to believe it.
- Kazehaya just wanted a

45
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:46,684
- girlfriend. That's all it is.
- Yeah.

46
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:49,354
I'm sure they'll break up soon.

47
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:50,772
My position...

48
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,566
And my feelings...

49
00:03:54,984 --> 00:03:59,364
- Those two are officially dating now.
- It makes me feel kinda lonely.

50
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:03,826
I'm honestly glad no one's come out
to attack Sawako over this whole thing.

51
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:07,413
- Yeah.
- And no one's tried to mess with

52
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:11,042
- her like that one group did before.
- That's true.

53
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:17,840
If anything, there may be
some girls crying in secret.

54
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:22,303
Yeah, I can definitely
understand having a reaction like that.

55
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:30,103
- Look, it's not what you think.
- None of it means we think

56
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:32,188
you're to blame for any of that!

57
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:34,315
No, I know you're right.

58
00:04:38,236 --> 00:04:41,948
I was overjoyed,
because it felt like a dream.

59
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:45,326
Kazehaya's face kept
showing up in my mind.

60
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:49,122
But what showed up next...

61
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:51,332
...was Kurumi's face.

62
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:58,256
Not only her... but the many other
people who were shocked by it.

63
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:03,720
All of their feelings are the exact
same as mine from not that long ago.

64
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:07,307
And I'm fully aware that they're
something produced because of the position

65
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:10,393
- I'm in now.
- I got rejected... but I

66
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:13,438
clearly told him my feelings.

67
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:16,899
If she never said those words...

68
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:20,236
If she was never there...

69
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,363
I think you mean rivals.

70
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:26,826
Sawa...

71
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,620
- I'm sorry, I need to go.
- Wait a sec, going where?!

72
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,914
Let her go, Chizu.

73
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,334
She's gonna see Kurumi.

74
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:37,879
Sawako!

75
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:42,050
I'll say this only 'cause I get how she
feels. There isn't anything you can do

76
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:45,303
about how it ended up for her.

77
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:46,429
You're not to blame.

78
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,724
Just don't forget that, okay?

79
00:05:55,104 --> 00:05:58,274
- And I know... she's gotta get her closure.
- Chizu sure does love

80
00:05:58,358 --> 00:06:01,444
her closure, doesn't she?

81
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:04,697
- Yeah.
- His girlfriend? Seriously?

82
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:09,494
That rumor's been around for a while.

83
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:12,914
If we knew this was gonna happen,
we would've been tougher on her.

84
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:16,084
Do you guys think we should let her know?

85
00:06:18,252 --> 00:06:20,922
Gonna tell us what's so funny, Kurumi?

86
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:26,052
This is why Kazehaya never liked you.

87
00:06:26,719 --> 00:06:30,056
- Are you trying to pick a fight?
- In case you've forgotten, you were

88
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:33,976
the one who started Sadako's rumor!

89
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:37,563
And then you used us to
benefit yourself didn't you?

90
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:41,234
- Yeah, and?
- The five of you were the perfect pawns.

91
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:45,113
Since you seemed
basically as rotten as I was.

92
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:50,201
It's too hard for you to ask Kazehaya
out yourself, so you pick on Sawako

93
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:55,248
- because it's a lot easier.
- Excuse me? You're no different than us!

94
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,251
Yeah, you're right.

95
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:01,295
Everyone but Sawako is just the same.

96
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:16,769
Kurumi...

97
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,276
Sadako!

98
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:26,571
So, are the rumors
about Kazehaya real or fake?

99
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:28,573
- They just can't be true!
- I don't believe it!

100
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:30,616
- Are you blackmailing him?!
- Uh, I don't...

101
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,535
I bet Yano and Yoshida helped you!

102
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:34,495
Why would he choose someone
like you, when he could have--

103
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,580
Shut up!

104
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:39,292
Give it a rest already.

105
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:45,214
Isn't it pathetic to still complain at
this point? This is what Kazehaya chose.

106
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:50,094
What? Who do you think you are?

107
00:07:50,261 --> 00:07:54,223
You think you're in a position to say
that? After everything you did?! -You know

108
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:58,227
what'll happen if we tell him,
don't you? -Go ahead and do it...

109
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:01,814
If you don't care what he thinks of you
after doing that then be my guest! He'll

110
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:05,443
ask you why you even brought it up.

111
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:09,071
And then see right through your ulterior
motives. He despises people who snitch on

112
00:08:09,155 --> 00:08:13,618
others just for their
own benefit. Understand?

113
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:18,080
And to add to that...

114
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:20,750
if you do anything to Sawako...

115
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:23,377
You're done for. He won't forgive you.

116
00:08:26,088 --> 00:08:28,174
And I... know that for a fact.

117
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:36,516
Get back here! I'm not done talking to--

118
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:43,231
Since I'm already her
rival... I'll talk to her.

119
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:51,656
What... Hey! Don't get carried
away just because you're his--

120
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,908
- Yo!
- Y-Yoshida.

121
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:59,330
- So, you still like Kazehaya, huh?
- Yeah, I still do. What about it?

122
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:02,083
Hold on a minute, does
this mean you all liked him?

123
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:04,877
- And why'd it have to be Sadako?
- I can't believe he's

124
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:07,672
taken by somebody now!

125
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:10,299
Huh?! You can't be
serious? Why didn't you tell me?!

126
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:11,217
"Why"?

127
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:14,262
Because we felt bad.

128
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:16,722
Y-You didn't know this beforehand?

129
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,474
Now, tell me...

130
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:23,396
Would you have given up easier if it was
Kurumi? Or would it have been better if

131
00:09:23,479 --> 00:09:27,191
Kazehaya had picked
one of you guys instead?

132
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:30,069
Either of those still would have been
hard, right? There's nothing wrong with

133
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:32,947
you guys still liking him.

134
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:38,119
But having said that, liking him for
a long time doesn't make you better.

135
00:09:38,744 --> 00:09:40,621
If you never take action...

136
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:42,873
You'll never get closure.

137
00:09:43,874 --> 00:09:48,004
The regret you're feeling is
because you didn't do anything.

138
00:09:48,087 --> 00:09:54,010
So isn't it messed up to complain
to Sawako while ignoring that fact?

139
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:57,847
And besides, Kazehaya
said this is a like a drea--

140
00:09:57,930 --> 00:10:01,767
Before all of this happened the way it
did, I'm pretty sure none of you had any

141
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:05,313
sort of problem with Sawako.

142
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:09,817
You just liked Kazehaya. And
that's all there was to it...

143
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:13,070
Regardless of his reputation or anything.

144
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:16,949
Well, that's probably the same with
Kazehaya. He's not the kinda guy to choose

145
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:20,828
someone based on reputation, right?

146
00:10:20,911 --> 00:10:25,082
I imagine you came to like him because
that's the way he is. But I don't need to

147
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:29,545
tell you that since you already know.

148
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:34,091
You're angry, but still, you all
want him to be happy don't you?

149
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:36,719
It's complicated.

150
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:42,183
There's no need to be
stubborn. Why not let it all out?

151
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:45,645
And don't do it for Kazehaya...

152
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:47,063
Do it for yourself.

153
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:00,993
P.E. TEACHER'S OFFICE

154
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:03,704
Hey, Shota. Way to go.

155
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:06,832
I mean, you helped.

156
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:09,293
Huh? But I don't think
I really did anything.

157
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:11,962
No, you lent me an ear--

158
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:13,047
Where's my thanks?

159
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,008
Well, Shota?

160
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:19,303
No matter how you look at it, I'm the MVP
here. I deserve a nice, "Thank you very

161
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:20,221
much!"

162
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,476
Yeah, you're right.

163
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:30,564
Despite everything, you actually did
help me to think through all that stuff

164
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:32,149
so... ...thanks.

165
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:35,277
Yeah, exactly!

166
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:40,866
And! Wanna know somethin'? I was also
giving Kuronuma some helpful advice behind

167
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:45,246
- your back at the exact same time!
- Who even asked you to do that?!

168
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:47,248
Please... don't give Kuronuma
any more unnecessary advice.

169
00:11:47,331 --> 00:11:48,165
Huh?

170
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,670
I want to take care of her, seriously.

171
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:57,842
I'm happy for ya, Shota. You were able to
squeeze out your measly feelings for her.

172
00:11:57,925 --> 00:12:01,262
You not listening, are you?

173
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:03,389
Hey, kiddo...

174
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:07,852
When it comes to romance, only the
person who asks someone out first, can

175
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:11,480
fight against their true love.

176
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:19,280
And the people who are second, third, or
beyond that, aren't even qualified for it.

177
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:21,031
Which means...

178
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:23,701
Whenever Kuronuma's true love shows up,
you're really gonna have to prove

179
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:26,454
- yourself.
- What are you talking about?

180
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:28,998
Shota... Hang in there.

181
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:43,596
What?

182
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:51,020
I... finally told my feelings to Kazehaya.

183
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,024
And we've decided to date.

184
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:04,784
Okay? Did you come here to brag?

185
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:11,207
If she were in my place, I'm sure
she would've done the same thing.

186
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:15,461
I told you, I'll never
say, "I'm happy for you."

187
00:13:17,379 --> 00:13:20,341
I know it. She'd have done it for me.

188
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:28,140
Anything else?

189
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:30,893
No.

190
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:32,978
Just wanted... you to know.

191
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:46,700
Sawako.

192
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:50,287
Do you remember?

193
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:54,583
When I had mentioned that
"I made sure to tell him"?

194
00:13:57,878 --> 00:14:00,339
It was only because you were there.

195
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:07,429
I think that if you hadn't been...

196
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:12,893
Then, I... would've never been
able to tell him my true feelings.

197
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:18,524
Despite getting rejected.

198
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:30,870
I'm glad...

199
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:35,249
...that you were my rival.

200
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:49,847
PLUM JUICE

201
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,985
You know... I overheard that

202
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,823
Your conversation with Sadako.

203
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:09,992
Your point?

204
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:13,537
Well, I just thought it
was surprising, is all.

205
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:17,291
That's true. It looked like she
was prepared to get told off by me.

206
00:15:17,374 --> 00:15:20,127
- And I intended to do so.
- Oh. Really?

207
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:24,632
But she didn't say anything. It was weird.

208
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:29,762
If she had said, "Thank you," or,
"I'm sorry," or something, I was honestly

209
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:33,557
- thinking of kicking her butt.
- Here's a question for you... what if I

210
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:37,186
went out with Sadako? What are your
thoughts on something like that?

211
00:15:37,269 --> 00:15:41,732
You're not good enough. That's mean.

212
00:15:43,567 --> 00:15:45,194
But neither am I.

213
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:53,869
If Kazehaya liked me, he
would've asked me out a long time ago.

214
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:57,039
Didn't matter how hard I tried.

215
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:59,875
In fact, whenever he was with her...

216
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,961
...he acted completely different.

217
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:08,133
I never knew he could
make a face like that.

218
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:12,221
Or that he could even
behave the way he did.

219
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,140
It's obvious now.

220
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:21,063
There's absolutely no chance Kazehaya
will ever like me from this point forward.

221
00:16:21,146 --> 00:16:26,110
I did the one thing that he hates the
most... and could never forgive me for.

222
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:31,740
To be honest, he couldn't handle you.

223
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:36,954
Y'know, truthfully, if I
liked girls, you'd be my type.

224
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:40,958
I mean it I know I could
understand you. Even all your darker

225
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:41,875
sides.

226
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:50,634
I don't need... sympathy.

227
00:16:54,805 --> 00:17:00,853
When I realized that this was finally
going to be over... I felt a bit relieved.

228
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:08,944
Oh yeah the whole thing surprised me...

229
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:12,823
Kazehaya was head over heels for Sadako.
And Kurumi was more awkward than I thought

230
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:14,033
she'd be.

231
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:21,707
On the flip side, Sadako was cuter than I
thought. Although, the biggest surprise

232
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:27,129
was me thinking, "I'm glad this all
happened before I started liking her."

233
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:28,881
Are you for real?!

234
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,090
Yeah, sure am.

235
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:32,718
I'm gonna need you to promise you
won't mess with her anymore, you got it?

236
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:35,554
Don't worry, I promise!

237
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:41,894
- What's that supposed to mean?
- I... couldn't say anything.

238
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:47,775
There was nothing that felt
right to say in that moment.

239
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:51,570
If it'd been me I
probably would've done the same.

240
00:17:51,653 --> 00:17:54,573
There's nothing you really can say to her.

241
00:17:55,365 --> 00:17:57,451
It's because of Kurumi...

242
00:17:58,077 --> 00:18:00,412
If she wasn't there then...

243
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:03,499
I wouldn't have had such a good rival.

244
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:06,835
And that's how I really feel.

245
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:10,964
But I know this isn't
something I should say out loud.

246
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:11,882
Ryu!

247
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:16,345
- See ya later, Sawa!
- Why?

248
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,055
Just come on!

249
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:21,100
- See ya, Shota.
- Later...

250
00:18:23,894 --> 00:18:25,104
Oh. Now I get it.

251
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:29,775
- Glad you figured it out.
- Yeah. By the way, Chizuru.

252
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:30,901
I like you.

253
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:36,657
- What the... Ryu! You surprised me!
- Thought you should know.

254
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:40,452
You big dummy! I already know!

255
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:48,460
There are all kinds of feelings... for
all kinds of people... in many situations...

256
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:53,674
- I'll see you tomorrow.
- Yeah.

257
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:03,392
Kazehaya!

258
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:06,228
Huh?

259
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:09,731
Nevermind...

260
00:19:11,775 --> 00:19:12,693
It's nothing.

261
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:17,614
I'm glad... that you were my rival.

262
00:19:21,702 --> 00:19:23,453
I'll treat him well.

263
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,458
I'll do my best

